# Refract — Campaign

Campaign is one of the two ways to play Refract, reached from the `CAMPAIGN` item
on the title menu. It is a course of `CAMPAIGN_LENGTH` (`24`) hand-built boards
worked through in order. The player opens one board at a time, draws the beams the
rules in `specs/beams.md` allow, and moves on once the board is solved. The other
way to play is the endless sequence in `specs/modes/cascade.md`, which the title
menu offers alongside this one.

Every board, its position in the course, and the order the player meets them
in are fixed.

This file defines the course, its progression, and the three screens the course
adds. The rules a board is solved under are in `specs/beams.md`, the grid and the
notation in `specs/board.md`, the tracing controls in `specs/controls.md`, the
`title`, `howto`, and `playing` screens in `specs/ui.md`, and what the game's
state carries in `specs/state.md`. Every figure and every piece of screen copy
below carries the name this specification gives it.

## Entering the campaign

- Choosing `CAMPAIGN` on the title menu sets `state.mode` to `"campaign"` and
  goes to `select`.
- Campaign progress lasts the session. Returning to `title` and entering the
  campaign again shows the same grid, with the same boards unlocked and solved.

## The twenty-four boards

- The course holds exactly `CAMPAIGN_LENGTH` (`24`) boards, numbered `1` through
  `24` in the order `specs/campaign-boards.md` lists them.
- `specs/campaign-boards.md` is **authoritative for every board's layout**. It
  gives each board's dimensions and its cells in the notation `specs/board.md`
  defines. Build each board exactly as written there. Do not substitute, reorder,
  resize, or rework a board.
- The `24` boards fall into four sets of six, labelled as
  `specs/campaign-boards.md` labels them:

  | Set | Boards |
  | --- | --- |
  | A | `1`–`6` |
  | B | `7`–`12` |
  | C | `13`–`18` |
  | D | `19`–`24` |

  A set is a grouping the select screen shows and labels. It has no gate of its
  own: the unlock rule below is the only thing that governs what a player can
  enter.

## Progression

- Board `1` is unlocked from the start. Every other board begins locked.
- Solving a board unlocks the next board by number: solving board `n` unlocks
  board `n + 1`.
- A board stays unlocked, and stays marked solved, for the rest of the session, so
  the player can return to any board already reached.
- Solving a board that is already solved changes no unlock state. It is a replay.
- Entering a board always starts it with every beam empty, whether it is a first
  attempt or a replay. Progress is per board and is never partially banked.
- Progress is not carried between sessions. A fresh start begins with board `1`
  unlocked and nothing solved.

